            <div class="tfa-seq-rail"><span class="tfa-seq-dot"></span></div>
            <blockquote class="tfa-seq-quote">"He did not sleep at night. He tried not to think about Ikemefuna, but the more he tried the more he thought about him. Once he got up from bed and walked about his compound. But he was so weak that his legs could hardly carry him. He felt like a drunken giant walking with the limbs of a mosquito."</blockquote>
          </article>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>The killing of Ikemefuna is the hinge of this strand of the novel's meaning. The Oracle decrees Ikemefuna must die. Ogbuefi Ezeudu tells Okonkwo he has no obligation to participate, but he participates anyway, "because he was afraid of being thought weak." He strikes the killing blow on a boy who called him "father" because his definition of strength has no space for the act of stepping aside.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>The night that follows — unable to sleep, thinking of Ezinma as the daughter who "should have been a boy," yet unable to grieve for Ikemefuna — is the novel's earliest and most precise measurement of what the masculine ideal extracts from the men who embody it. His tragedy is simultaneously personal and cultural: the novel suggests that the same values that made Igbo civilization great also produced a structure with built-in vulnerabilities that colonialism could exploit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <ZoneSeam text="tfa" groundFrom="cream" groundTo="tinted" />

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ZONE 4 — The Fault Lines of Igbo Culture · ground · still · tinted
       Combines the church section with Okonkwo's death.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="sr-scrolly-zone sr-scrolly-zone--ground" data-field="ground" data-tempo="still" data-ground="tinted" data-text="tfa" data-screen-label="§4 The Fault Lines of Igbo Culture">
    <div class="sr-zone-ground-content">

      <SectionOpener text="tfa" eyebrow="Conversion and Tragedy" heading="The Fault Lines of Igbo Culture" background="tinted" motifIdx={4} />

      <figure class="sr-pullquote sr-pullquote--tfa tfa-zone-pull">
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--top" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
        <blockquote class="sr-pullquote-body"><p>"It was not the mad logic of the Trinity that captivated him. It was the poetry of the new religion, something felt in the marrow."</p></blockquote>
        <figcaption class="sr-pullquote-attribution">— Things Fall Apart, Chinua Achebe</figcaption>
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--bottom" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
      </figure>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body tfa-passage-body--lede">
          <p>The arrival of the missionaries in Umuofia is often read as straightforwardly destructive, but Achebe's rendering of their insinuation into Umuofian society is more uncomfortable than that. The church does dismantle Igbo governance and cosmology systematically, but it begins with personal conversions, and those conversions are not irrational.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="tfa-margin-fig" aria-label="An ideogram of the church and the margins: the clan, a closed terracotta ring around its titled centre, pushes three small rings to its edge; the open green ring beside it, marked with a cross, receives them.">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 240 200" class="tfa-margin-svg" role="img" aria-label="A closed terracotta ring around a titled centre of three dots in a small ring holds three small rings at its edge; an open green ring on the right, holding a cross, receives them.">
          <circle cx="80" cy="100" r="44" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.4"></circle>
          <circle cx="80" cy="100" r="9.5" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="1.3" opacity="0.6"></circle>
          <circle cx="77" cy="102" r="1.9" fill="var(--t-terra)"></circle>
          <circle cx="83" cy="102" r="1.9" fill="var(--t-terra)"></circle>
          <circle cx="80" cy="96.5" r="1.9" fill="var(--t-terra)"></circle>
          <circle cx="122" cy="74" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.2"></circle>
          <circle cx="128" cy="100" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.2"></circle>
          <circle cx="122" cy="126" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.2"></circle>
          <path d="M136.1 81.4 A44 44 0 1 1 136.1 118.6" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-forest)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <line x1="180" y1="84" x2="180" y2="118" stroke="var(--t-forest)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
          <line x1="170" y1="94" x2="190" y2="94" stroke="var(--t-forest)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="tfa-margin-cap">
          <span class="tfa-margin-key">The clan · the margins · the church</span>
          The clan closes around its titled centre and pushes others to its edge. The church is the open ring — marked by the cross — that receives exactly those the circle excluded: <em>Nwoye, the osu, the mothers of twins.</em>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>Nwoye hears a Christian hymn and feels something yield inside him — the poetry of the new religion. He cannot meet the demands of Igbo masculine achievement; his father's version of what a man is has been a crushing weight since childhood. The church offers him a different set of values and a community that does not judge him by his father's standards. His conversion is as much an escape from Okonkwo as it is an embrace of Christianity. The <em>osu</em> — the outcast class — find in the church the offer of inclusion they have never experienced. So do the mothers of twins, whose children were left to die in the Evil Forest. The church welcomes those the Igbo system has excluded.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-pivot" data-screen-label="§4 pivot sentence">
        <p>Colonialism succeeded in Igboland partly by embracing the people that Igbo culture had already marginalized. The disruption worked through existing fault lines, and some of those fault lines were real moral failures.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="sr-pullquote sr-pullquote--tfa tfa-zone-pull">
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--top" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
        <blockquote class="sr-pullquote-body"><p>"He heard voices asking: 'Why did he do it?'"</p></blockquote>
        <figcaption class="sr-pullquote-attribution">— Things Fall Apart, Chinua Achebe (after Okonkwo kills the court messenger)</figcaption>
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--bottom" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="tfa-seq" aria-label="The death of Okonkwo — a four-beat sequence with quotations from Things Fall Apart, chapters 24 and 25">
        <figcaption class="tfa-seq-head">
          <span class="tfa-seq-eyebrow">The death of Okonkwo · a sequence</span>
          <span class="tfa-seq-eyebrow tfa-seq-eyebrow--muted">Chinua Achebe · ch. 24–25</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="tfa-seq-track">
          <div class="tfa-seq-phase">The act</div>
          <article class="tfa-seq-beat">
            <span class="tfa-seq-kicker">The confrontation</span>
            <div class="tfa-seq-glyph">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 200 168" class="tfa-seq-svg" role="img" aria-label="Okonkwo, a terracotta mark trembling with hate, faces a line of four dark uniformed messengers and the order they carry.">
                <circle cx="52" cy="86" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.4"></circle>
                <g stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <line x1="40" y1="70" x2="33" y2="62"></line>
                  <line x1="52" y1="66" x2="52" y2="56"></line>
                  <line x1="64" y1="70" x2="71" y2="62"></line>
                  <line x1="52" y1="98" x2="52" y2="120"></line>
                </g>
                <line x1="118" y1="86" x2="82" y2="86" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 4" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <path d="M88 81 L80 86 L88 91" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
                <g stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <line x1="130" y1="70" x2="130" y2="110"></line>
                  <line x1="146" y1="70" x2="146" y2="110"></line>
                  <line x1="162" y1="70" x2="162" y2="110"></line>
                  <line x1="178" y1="70" x2="178" y2="110"></line>
                </g>
                <g stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <line x1="124" y1="64" x2="136" y2="64"></line>
                  <line x1="140" y1="64" x2="152" y2="64"></line>
                  <line x1="156" y1="64" x2="168" y2="64"></line>
                  <line x1="172" y1="64" x2="184" y2="64"></line>
                </g>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="tfa-seq-rail"><span class="tfa-seq-dot"></span></div>
            <blockquote class="tfa-seq-quote">"What do you want here?" "The white man whose power you know too well has ordered this meeting to stop."</blockquote>
          </article>
          <article class="tfa-seq-beat">
            <span class="tfa-seq-kicker">The blow</span>
            <div class="tfa-seq-glyph">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 200 168" class="tfa-seq-svg" role="img" aria-label="Two heavy dark machete strokes descend; a severed round head lies beside a short uniformed body.">
                <g stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <line x1="110" y1="92" x2="126" y2="88" stroke-width="2.2"></line>
                  <line x1="108" y1="98" x2="120" y2="106" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.8"></line>
                </g>
                <line x1="70" y1="44" x2="104" y2="92" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="6.5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <line x1="84" y1="38" x2="118" y2="86" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="6.5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <circle cx="138" cy="104" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="2.6"></circle>
                <line x1="150" y1="120" x2="178" y2="120" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <line x1="156" y1="113" x2="156" y2="120" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="tfa-seq-rail"><span class="tfa-seq-dot"></span></div>
            <blockquote class="tfa-seq-quote">"In a flash Okonkwo drew his machete. The messenger crouched to avoid the blow. It was useless. Okonkwo's machete descended twice and the man's head lay beside his uniformed body."</blockquote>
          </article>
          <div class="tfa-seq-phase">The aftermath</div>
          <article class="tfa-seq-beat">
            <span class="tfa-seq-kicker">He stood alone</span>
            <div class="tfa-seq-glyph">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 200 168" class="tfa-seq-svg" role="img" aria-label="A single terracotta figure stands at the centre while a ring of grey figures scatters outward, leaving a gap.">
                <g stroke="var(--color-muted)" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.6">
                  <g><circle cx="100" cy="22" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none"></circle><line x1="100" y1="18" x2="100" y2="9" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="150" cy="40" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none"></circle><line x1="153" y1="37" x2="161" y2="29" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="172" cy="84" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none" opacity="0.85"></circle><line x1="176" y1="84" x2="186" y2="84" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="150" cy="128" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none" opacity="0.7"></circle><line x1="153" y1="131" x2="161" y2="139" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="50" cy="40" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none"></circle><line x1="47" y1="37" x2="39" y2="29" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="28" cy="84" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none" opacity="0.85"></circle><line x1="24" y1="84" x2="14" y2="84" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                  <g><circle cx="50" cy="128" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)" stroke="none" opacity="0.7"></circle><line x1="47" y1="131" x2="39" y2="139" stroke-width="1.4"></line></g>
                </g>
                <circle cx="100" cy="74" r="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.4"></circle>
                <line x1="100" y1="80" x2="100" y2="104" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <line x1="88" y1="90" x2="112" y2="90" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="tfa-seq-rail"><span class="tfa-seq-dot"></span></div>
            <blockquote class="tfa-seq-quote">"He knew that Umuofia would not go to war. He knew because they had let the other messengers escape. They had broken into tumult instead of action. He heard voices asking: 'Why did he do it?'"</blockquote>
          </article>
          <article class="tfa-seq-beat">
            <span class="tfa-seq-kicker">Against the earth</span>
            <div class="tfa-seq-glyph">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 200 168" class="tfa-seq-svg" role="img" aria-label="A body hangs by a rope from a branch; below it a dashed terracotta earth-line it does not reach, the gap barred.">
                <line x1="60" y1="28" x2="140" y2="28" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <path d="M122 28 q6 -8 13 -6" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7"></path>
                <path d="M78 28 q-5 -7 -12 -5" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7"></path>
                <line x1="100" y1="28" x2="100" y2="96" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
                <circle cx="100" cy="104" r="7" fill="none" stroke="var(--t-umber)" stroke-width="2.4"></circle>
                <line x1="100" y1="114" x2="100" y2="130" stroke="var(--color-muted)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="2 4" opacity="0.6"></line>
                <line x1="92" y1="123" x2="108" y2="123" stroke="var(--color-muted)" stroke-width="1.3" opacity="0.6"></line>
                <line x1="34" y1="144" x2="166" y2="144" stroke="var(--t-terra)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="5 4"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="tfa-seq-rail"><span class="tfa-seq-dot"></span></div>
            <blockquote class="tfa-seq-quote">"That man was one of the greatest men in Umuofia. You drove him to kill himself; and now he will be buried like a dog…" He could not say any more. His voice trembled and choked his words.</blockquote>
          </article>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>Okonkwo's tragedy operates on two levels that the novel refuses to separate. At the personal level, he is a man whose values served him in the traditional world of Umuofia but become lethal liabilities in the world colonialism has made. At the cultural level, his death represents the impossibility of resistance on Igbo cultural terms. He kills a court messenger and looks around to find that no one is following him. The world that made those values coherent has already fallen apart before Okonkwo acts. His suicide by hanging is itself an offense against Ala — he dies in a way that denies him proper burial in the earth he spent his life honoring. The Igbo world that Okonkwo once embodied cannot accommodate the manner of his dying.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>What falls apart is specific: village autonomy, the egwugwu courts, the Oracle's judicial authority, the binding force of Ala, the communal solidarity between converts and non-converts. What survives — implicitly, through the act of writing — is the history itself.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <ZoneSeam text="tfa" groundFrom="tinted" groundTo="cream" />

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ZONE 5 — A Reasonable Paragraph · book · driving · cream
       The spoke's single earned visual: cover → paragraph → response.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="sr-scrolly-zone tfa-zone--book" data-field="book" data-tempo="driving" data-ground="cream" data-text="tfa" data-screen-label="§5 A Reasonable Paragraph">

    <div class="tfa-z4-intro">
      <SectionOpener text="tfa" eyebrow="The Last Page" heading="A Reasonable Paragraph" background="cream" motifIdx={4} />
    </div>

    <div class="sr-zone-field tfa-book-field" data-reveal="exclusive">
      <div class="tfa-book-layer" data-show-from="book-cover">
        <svg data-book-cover xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A plain, institutional colonial-era book, its cover facing the reader. The title reads, in full: The Pacification of the Primitive Tribes of the Lower Niger, by the District Commissioner."></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="tfa-book-layer" data-show-from="book-paragraph">
        <svg data-book-paragraph xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The same book, open. Both pages are dense with indistinct administrative prose. One small paragraph on the right page is marked; the only legible words in it read 'a reasonable paragraph'."></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="tfa-book-layer" data-show-from="book-response">
        <svg data-book-response xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The Commissioner's volume now stands beside a second book, the same size: Things Fall Apart, by Chinua Achebe. The two covers face the reader together, unlabeled. The juxtaposition is the argument."></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="tfa-book-caption"><em>The Pacification of the Primitive Tribes of the Lower Niger</em> — the title of the District Commissioner's book, as recorded on the final page of <em>Things Fall Apart</em>. The book does not exist. Achebe invented it to show what the colonial archive does to a human life.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sr-zone-beats">
      <div class="sr-zone-beat sr-zone-beat--left" data-beat data-activates="book-cover">
        <div class="sr-beat-card"><p>The novel's last page is one of the most precisely calibrated endings in twentieth-century fiction. The District Commissioner walks away from Okonkwo's hanging body. He will not cut it down himself — a district commissioner does not attend to such undignified details. He thinks about his book. Every day in Africa brings him material. Okonkwo's story is interesting. One could almost write a whole chapter about him. "Perhaps not a whole chapter but a reasonable paragraph, at any rate."</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sr-zone-beat sr-zone-beat--center" data-beat data-activates="book-paragraph">
        <div class="sr-beat-card"><p>Achebe has given the reader two hundred pages of Okonkwo's life: his wrestling match at eighteen, his yam barns, his three wives, his love for Ezinma, his killing of Ikemefuna, his exile, his return, his inability to find anyone to fight alongside him, his death. The District Commissioner will give it a paragraph.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sr-zone-beat sr-zone-beat--right" data-beat data-activates="book-response">
        <div class="sr-beat-card"><p>The contrast is the argument. This is what the colonial gaze does to human life: reduces it to administrative material, strips it of interiority and history and tragedy, files it under a title that encodes every assumption the novel has spent two hundred pages dismantling. The District Commissioner is not cruel in any obvious personal sense. That is precisely the point. He considers himself a reasonable man doing important work. <strong>Achebe wrote the novel to give Okonkwo back his two hundred pages — to restore the </strong><em>kleos</em><strong>, the glory-in-song that an epic hero is owed and that the colonial archive reduces to a paragraph.</strong> The book Okonkwo deserves is the one we have just read; the one the District Commissioner will write is the one Achebe wrote against.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

  <ZoneSeam text="tfa" groundFrom="cream" groundTo="tinted" />

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ZONE 6 — Achebe and the Western Canon · ground · still · tinted
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="sr-scrolly-zone sr-scrolly-zone--ground" data-field="ground" data-tempo="still" data-ground="tinted" data-text="tfa" data-screen-label="§6 Achebe and Yeats">
    <div class="sr-zone-ground-content">

      <SectionOpener text="tfa" eyebrow="The Epigraph" heading="Achebe and the Western Canon" background="tinted" motifIdx={4} />

      <figure class="sr-pullquote sr-pullquote--tfa tfa-zone-pull tfa-verse">
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--top" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
        <blockquote class="sr-pullquote-body"><p>Turning and turning in the widening gyre<br />The falcon cannot hear the falconer;<br />Things fall apart; the centre cannot hold;<br />Mere anarchy is loosed upon the world.</p></blockquote>
        <figcaption class="sr-pullquote-attribution">— W. B. Yeats, "The Second Coming" (1919)</figcaption>
        <div class="sr-pullquote-bracket sr-pullquote-bracket--bottom" aria-hidden="true"><UliTendril width={80} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.7} /></div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="tfa-gyre-fig" aria-label="Yeats's widening gyre: a spiral that widens with every turn, leaving its fixed centre behind.">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 240 200" class="tfa-gyre-svg" role="img" aria-label="A spiral that widens with every turn around a small fixed centre point; a small arrowhead at the open end shows it spinning outward.">
          <path d="M125.0 100.0 L125.5 100.8 L125.8 101.7 L126.0 102.7 L126.0 103.7 L125.8 104.9 L125.4 106.0 L124.8 107.1 L124.0 108.2 L122.9 109.2 L121.7 110.0 L120.3 110.7 L118.8 111.1 L117.1 111.3 L115.4 111.3 L113.6 111.0 L111.8 110.4 L110.1 109.5 L108.4 108.3 L106.9 106.8 L105.6 105.1 L104.5 103.2 L103.7 101.0 L103.2 98.7 L103.1 96.2 L103.3 93.7 L103.9 91.2 L104.8 88.7 L106.2 86.4 L107.9 84.2 L110.0 82.2 L112.4 80.5 L115.1 79.1 L118.0 78.1 L121.1 77.5 L124.3 77.4 L127.6 77.7 L130.8 78.6 L134.0 79.9 L137.0 81.6 L139.8 83.9 L142.3 86.5 L144.5 89.6 L146.2 92.9 L147.4 96.6 L148.1 100.5 L148.3 104.5 L147.9 108.5 L146.9 112.6 L145.3 116.5 L143.2 120.2 L140.4 123.6 L137.2 126.7 L133.6 129.3 L129.5 131.4 L125.1 132.9 L120.5 133.8 L115.7 134.0 L110.8 133.6 L106.0 132.5 L101.4 130.6 L97.0 128.1 L92.9 125.0 L89.2 121.3 L86.1 117.0 L83.6 112.3 L81.7 107.2 L80.6 101.8 L80.2 96.2 L80.6 90.6 L81.9 85.0 L83.9 79.5 L86.7 74.4 L90.2 69.6 L94.4 65.4 L99.3 61.7 L104.7 58.7 L110.5 56.4 L116.6 55.0 L122.9 54.5 L129.4 54.8 L135.8 56.1 L142.0 58.3 L147.9 61.3 L153.4 65.2 L158.3 69.9 L162.6 75.3 L166.1 81.3 L168.7 87.7 L170.5 94.6 L171.2 101.7 L171.0 108.9 L169.8 116.1 L167.5 123.1 L164.2 129.8 L160.0 136.1 L154.9 141.7 L149.0 146.6 L142.4 150.6 L135.3 153.8 L127.7 155.9 L119.8 156.9 L111.8 156.9 L103.8 155.7 L96.0 153.3 L88.5 149.9 L81.5 145.4 L75.2 139.9 L69.6 133.6 L65.0 126.4 L61.3 118.7 L58.8 110.4 L57.4 101.7 L57.3 92.9 L58.4 84.1 L60.7 75.5 L64.3 67.2 L69.0 59.4 L74.8 52.3 L81.6 46.1 L89.3 40.8 L97.7 36.6 L106.6 33.6 L116.0 31.9 L125.6 31.5 L135.2 32.4 L144.7 34.7 L153.8 38.3 L162.4 43.3 L170.2 49.4 L177.2 56.5 L183.2 64.7 L188.0 73.7 L191.5 83.3 L193.6 93.4 L194.3 103.8 L193.6 114.2 L191.4 124.5 L187.7 134.4 L182.7 143.8 L176.3 152.5 L168.8 160.2 L160.1 166.9 L150.6 172.3 L140.3 176.4 L129.6 179.0" fill="none" stroke="#41525E" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          <path d="M120 180 L130 175 M120 180 L130 185" stroke="#41525E" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <circle cx="120" cy="100" r="3" fill="var(--color-muted)"></circle>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="tfa-gyre-cap">
          <span class="tfa-gyre-key">Turning and turning · the widening gyre</span>
          Yeats's figure for history — a spiral that widens with every turn until the centre it spun from can no longer hold it. Achebe sets the same gyre spinning over <em>Umuofia.</em>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body tfa-passage-body--lede">
          <p>Achebe opens his novel with four lines from Yeats's "The Second Coming," written in the immediate aftermath of World War I. Yeats's poem is a vision of civilizational collapse — order dissolving, the falcon losing contact with the falconer, the center failing to hold. By choosing this epigraph, Achebe is making a claim before his novel has even begun.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>In Yeats, the center that cannot hold is European civilization; the collapse is the crisis of Western modernity. Achebe borrows the image and recontextualizes it entirely. In <em>Things Fall Apart</em>, the center that cannot hold is Umuofia — an African civilization, fully realized on its own terms, destroyed not by internal failure but by external force. The widening gyre is colonial encroachment. The falcon that cannot hear the falconer is Okonkwo, increasingly unable to orient himself within a world that no longer operates by its own rules.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-passage">
        <div class="tfa-passage-body">
          <p>The choice of a Yeats epigraph is itself an argument about literary authority. It is the same gesture made by the novel's epic opening, now at the scale of a single allusion. Invoking the form of the epic genre and borrowing Yeats's lines are two versions of one claim — that <em>Things Fall Apart</em> belongs in the conversation of the Western canon, on equal footing, while telling a story that canon had erased. Achebe is claiming the same weight of tragedy and civilizational stakes for Igbo civilization's collapse that Yeats assigned to the collapse of the European order. There is also a quiet irony in the choice: Yeats could not have imagined his poem about European crisis being repurposed as the frame for an African novel written in deliberate opposition to the assumptions of that same tradition. That act of appropriation is itself a form of the novel's argument — the tools of the colonial literary tradition can be used to tell the story of what that tradition erased.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tfa-end">
        <TriangleTerminator width={240} color="var(--t-terra)" opacity={0.9} />
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</SummerLayout>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';

  document.body.classList.add('tfa-pivot-isolated', 'tfa-dens-clean');

  /* ═══════════ Novel-structure bar ═══════════ */
  function buildNovelStructure() {
    var svg = document.querySelector('[data-novel-structure]');
    if (!svg) return;
    var x0 = 40, x1 = 720, top = 84, h = 30, seam = 470;
    var p = [];
    p.push('<rect class="ns-part1" x="' + x0 + '" y="' + top + '" width="' + (seam - x0) + '" height="' + h + '"/>');
    var items = [
      [90, 'the wrestling match'], [186, 'governance'], [282, 'cosmology'],
      [366, 'the harvest'], [440, 'the egwugwu']
    ];
    items.forEach(function (it) {
      p.push('<line class="ns-tick" x1="' + it[0] + '" y1="' + (top - 8) + '" x2="' + it[0] + '" y2="' + top + '"/>');
      p.push('<circle class="ns-node" cx="' + it[0] + '" cy="' + (top - 8) + '" r="3.2"/>');
    });
    p.push('<text class="ns-content" x="' + x0 + '" y="' + (top - 22) + '">' +
      'governance · cosmology · the agricultural year · the egwugwu courts · the Week of Peace</text>');
    p.push('<defs><linearGradient id="ns-grad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">' +
      '<stop offset="0" stop-color="#C4722A" stop-opacity="0.18"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2C1A08" stop-opacity="0.20"/></linearGradient></defs>');
    p.push('<rect x="' + seam + '" y="' + top + '" width="' + (x1 - seam) + '" height="' + h + '" fill="url(#ns-grad)" stroke="#2C1A08" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>');
    p.push('<rect class="ns-cool" x="' + (x1 - 16) + '" y="' + top + '" width="16" height="' + h + '" opacity="0.85"/>');
    p.push('<line class="ns-seam" x1="' + seam + '" y1="' + (top - 34) + '" x2="' + seam + '" y2="' + (top + h + 10) + '"/>');
    p.push('<circle class="ns-seam-dot" cx="' + seam + '" cy="' + (top - 34) + '" r="3"/>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-lbl ns-lbl--umber" x="' + (seam + 8) + '" y="' + (top - 30) + '">the missionaries arrive</text>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-sub" x="' + (seam + 8) + '" y="' + (top - 16) + '">— not until here</text>');
    var by = top + h + 16;
    p.push('<path class="ns-brace" d="M' + x0 + ' ' + by + ' L' + x0 + ' ' + (by + 6) + ' L' + seam + ' ' + (by + 6) + ' L' + seam + ' ' + by + '"/>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-lbl ns-lbl--terra" x="' + ((x0 + seam) / 2) + '" y="' + (by + 22) + '" text-anchor="middle">PART ONE</text>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-sub" x="' + ((x0 + seam) / 2) + '" y="' + (by + 38) + '" text-anchor="middle">a world built from the inside</text>');
    p.push('<path class="ns-brace ns-brace--umber" d="M' + seam + ' ' + by + ' L' + seam + ' ' + (by + 6) + ' L' + x1 + ' ' + (by + 6) + ' L' + x1 + ' ' + by + '"/>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-lbl ns-lbl--umber" x="' + ((seam + x1) / 2) + '" y="' + (by + 22) + '" text-anchor="middle">PARTS TWO &amp; THREE</text>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-sub" x="' + ((seam + x1) / 2) + '" y="' + (by + 38) + '" text-anchor="middle">disruption, and the closing paragraph</text>');
    p.push('<text class="ns-tag" x="' + x0 + '" y="' + (top - 44) + '">THE READER’S EXPERIENCE, IN ORDER</text>');
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox', '0 24 760 188');
    svg.innerHTML = p.join('');
  }

  /* ═══════════ District Commissioner's book ═══════════ */
  function poly(pts, cls) {
    return '<polygon class="' + cls + '" points="' + pts.map(function (p) { return p[0] + ',' + p[1]; }).join(' ') + '"/>';
  }

  function closedBook(x, y, w, h, o) {
    o = o || {};
    var d = o.depth || 10, cx = x + w / 2, fs = o.fontSize || 12, lh = fs + 5;
    var cov = o.coverClass || 'bk-cover', edge = o.edgeClass || 'bk-cover-edge', spn = o.spineClass || 'bk-spine';
    var tc = o.titleClass || 'bk-title', byc = o.byClass || 'bk-by';
    var s = [];
    s.push('<ellipse class="bk-shadow" cx="' + (cx + 3) + '" cy="' + (y + h + d + 8) + '" rx="' + (w * 0.52) + '" ry="6"/>');
    s.push(poly([[x + w, y + 4], [x + w + d, y + 4 + d], [x + w + d, y + h + d], [x + w, y + h]], edge));
    s.push(poly([[x + 4, y + h], [x + 4 + d, y + h + d], [x + w + d, y + h + d], [x + w, y + h]], edge));
    s.push('<rect class="' + cov + '" x="' + x + '" y="' + y + '" width="' + w + '" height="' + h + '" rx="2"/>');
    s.push('<rect class="' + spn + '" x="' + x + '" y="' + y + '" width="9" height="' + h + '" rx="1"/>');
    s.push('<rect class="bk-rule" x="' + (x + 18) + '" y="' + (y + 18) + '" width="' + (w - 30) + '" height="' + (h - 36) + '" fill="none"/>');
    s.push('<rect class="bk-rule--thin" x="' + (x + 22) + '" y="' + (y + 22) + '" width="' + (w - 38) + '" height="' + (h - 44) + '" fill="none"/>');
    var lines = o.titleLines || [];
    var startY = y + h * 0.40 - (lines.length - 1) * lh / 2;
    lines.forEach(function (ln, i) {
      s.push('<text class="' + tc + '" x="' + (cx + 4) + '" y="' + (startY + i * lh) + '" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:' + fs + 'px">' + ln + '</text>');
    });
    var ry = y + h * 0.40 + lines.length * lh / 2 + 14;
    s.push('<line class="bk-rule" x1="' + (cx - 22) + '" y1="' + ry + '" x2="' + (cx + 30) + '" y2="' + ry + '" opacity="0.6"/>');
    if (o.by) {
      o.by.forEach(function (bl, i) {
        s.push('<text class="' + byc + '" x="' + (cx + 4) + '" y="' + (ry + 18 + i * 11) + '" text-anchor="middle">' + bl + '</text>');
      });
    }
    if (o.uli) {
      s.push('<path class="bk-uli" d="M' + (cx - 18) + ' ' + (y + h - 26) + ' q 9 -10 18 0 q 9 10 18 0" transform="translate(-9,0)"/>');
    }
    return s.join('');
  }

  function buildBookCover() {
    var el = document.querySelector('[data-book-cover]');
    if (!el) return;
    el.setAttribute('viewBox', '0 0 300 380');
    el.innerHTML = closedBook(66, 44, 168, 292, {
      fontSize: 12,
      titleLines: ['THE', 'PACIFICATION', 'OF THE PRIMITIVE', 'TRIBES OF THE', 'LOWER NIGER'],
      by: ['BY THE', 'DISTRICT COMMISSIONER']
    });
  }

  function buildBookParagraph() {
    var el = document.querySelector('[data-book-paragraph]');
    if (!el) return;
    var p = [];
    p.push('<ellipse class="bk-shadow" cx="184" cy="300" rx="150" ry="7"/>');
    p.push(poly([[30, 56], [180, 46], [330, 56], [332, 286], [180, 296], [28, 286]], 'bk-cover'));
    p.push(poly([[40, 60], [180, 50], [180, 288], [40, 280]], 'bk-leaf'));
    p.push(poly([[180, 50], [320, 60], [320, 280], [180, 288]], 'bk-leaf'));
    p.push('<line class="bk-gutter" x1="180" y1="50" x2="180" y2="288"/>');
    function lines(xl, xrBase, yTop, n, seed) {
      var out = '', s = seed;
      for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        s = (s * 9301 + 49297) % 233280; var r = s / 233280;
        var y = yTop + i * 13.5;
        var w = (xrBase - xl) * (0.66 + r * 0.34);
        out += '<line class="bk-textline" x1="' + xl + '" y1="' + y.toFixed(1) + '" x2="' + (xl + w).toFixed(1) + '" y2="' + y.toFixed(1) + '"/>';
      }
      return out;
    }
    p.push(lines(54, 168, 74, 14, 7));
    p.push(lines(192, 306, 74, 6, 19));
    p.push('<rect class="bk-mark" x="190" y="160" width="120" height="58" rx="2"/>');
    p.push('<line class="bk-mark-line" x1="190" y1="160" x2="190" y2="218"/>');
    p.push('<line class="bk-textline" x1="196" y1="170" x2="300" y2="170"/>');
    p.push('<text class="bk-readable" x="250" y="193" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:12px">"a reasonable</text>');
    p.push('<text class="bk-readable" x="250" y="209" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:12px">paragraph"</text>');
    p.push(lines(192, 306, 230, 4, 41));
    p.push('<text class="bk-folio" x="160" y="278" text-anchor="end">208</text>');
    p.push('<text class="bk-folio" x="200" y="278">209</text>');
    el.setAttribute('viewBox', '0 30 360 290');
    el.innerHTML = p.join('');
  }

  function buildBookResponse() {
    var el = document.querySelector('[data-book-response]');
    if (!el) return;
    el.setAttribute('viewBox', '0 0 420 360');
    var left = closedBook(30, 70, 150, 250, {
      fontSize: 9.5,
      titleLines: ['THE PACIFICATION', 'OF THE PRIMITIVE', 'TRIBES OF THE', 'LOWER NIGER'],
      by: ['DISTRICT', 'COMMISSIONER']
    });
    var right = closedBook(232, 70, 150, 250, {
      fontSize: 11.5,
      coverClass: 'bk-cover--achebe', edgeClass: 'bk-cover-edge--achebe', spineClass: 'bk-spine--achebe',
      titleClass: 'bk-title bk-title--achebe', byClass: 'bk-by bk-by--achebe',
      titleLines: ['THINGS', 'FALL APART'],
      by: ['CHINUA ACHEBE'],
      uli: true
    });
    el.innerHTML = left + right;
  }

  function buildBook() {
    buildBookCover();
    buildBookParagraph();
    buildBookResponse();
  }

  /* ═══════════ Position-driven scrolly sweep (book zone) ═══════════ */
  var sweeps = [];
  var revealTween = null;
  var nextFrame = function (fn) { return document.hidden ? setTimeout(fn, 16) : requestAnimationFrame(fn); };

  function setFieldReveal(field, revealed) {
    var changed = false;
    field.querySelectorAll('[data-show-from]').forEach(function (g) {
      var target = revealed[g.getAttribute('data-show-from')] ? 1 : 0;
      if (g.__c === undefined) g.__c = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(g).opacity) || 0;
      if (g.__t !== target) { g.__t = target; changed = true; }
    });
    if (changed && !revealTween) revealTween = nextFrame(tickReveal);
  }

  function tickReveal() {
    revealTween = null;
    var moving = false;
    document.querySelectorAll('.tfa-book-field [data-show-from]').forEach(function (g) {
      if (g.__t === undefined) return;
      var cur = g.__c === undefined ? 0 : g.__c;
      var diff = g.__t - cur;
      if (Math.abs(diff) < 0.02) cur = g.__t; else { cur += diff * 0.16; moving = true; }
      g.__c = cur;
      g.style.opacity = String(cur);
    });
    if (moving) revealTween = nextFrame(tickReveal);
  }

  function initZones() {
    sweeps = [];
    var reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    var w = window.innerWidth;
    if (reduced || (w > 0 && w < 768)) return;

    document.querySelectorAll('.sr-scrolly-zone[data-field="book"]').forEach(function (zoneEl) {
      var field = zoneEl.querySelector('.sr-zone-field');
      var beats = Array.prototype.slice.call(zoneEl.querySelectorAll('[data-beat]'));
      if (!beats.length) return;

      function sweep() {
        var line = window.innerHeight * 0.5;
        var bestIdx = 0, bestDist = Infinity;
        beats.forEach(function (el, i) {
          var rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
          var mid = rect.top + rect.height / 2;
          var dist = Math.abs(mid - line);
          if (dist < bestDist) { bestDist = dist; bestIdx = i; }
        });
        beats.forEach(function (el, i) { el.classList.toggle('is-active', i === bestIdx); });
        if (field && field.querySelector('[data-show-from]')) {
          var revealed = {};
          var cur = beats[bestIdx] && beats[bestIdx].dataset.activates;
          if (cur) revealed[cur] = 1;
          setFieldReveal(field, revealed);
          field.querySelectorAll('[data-show-from]').forEach(function (g) {
            g.classList.toggle('is-current', !!cur && g.getAttribute('data-show-from') === cur);
          });
        }
      }
      sweeps.push(sweep);
      sweep();
    });
  }

  var queued = false;
  function runSweeps() {
    if (queued || !sweeps.length) return;
    queued = true;
    nextFrame(function () { queued = false; sweeps.forEach(function (fn) { fn(); }); });
  }

  function init() {
    buildNovelStructure();
    buildBook();
    initZones();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', runSweeps, { passive: true });
    var rt;
    window.addEventListener('resize', function () {
      clearTimeout(rt);
      rt = setTimeout(function () { initZones(); runSweeps(); }, 160);
    });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
  else init();
})();
</script>
